; sqlite — SQLite's own library behind a connection: scripts, prepared
; statements with text, integer, byte and NULL parameters, rows of text
; and bytes. The database is a file (or ":memory:"); a call into the
; library runs to its end on the calling thread -- there is no socket to
; park a task on, and a statement on a local file is short.
;
; A connection belongs to the thread that opened it.

package scaly 0.1.0

extern sqlite3

define sqlite
{
    module Conn
    module Thread
}
